r": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011X8USADUsBaWi2DrniGhhU", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 10580, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01KzyZBKpAaVtDbQP4ezymfb", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 10880, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01KzyZBKpAaVtDbQP4ezymfb", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 10880, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KzyZBKpAaVtDbQP4ezymfb", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 14094, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WXpdc8mNpfMXgZfHvwJnNX", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 18094, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WXpdc8mNpfMXgZfHvwJnNX", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18094, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WXpdc8mNpfMXgZfHvwJnNX", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19785, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01KwKATGfft9CLGcyYL34ZXW", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20085, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01KwKATGfft9CLGcyYL34ZXW", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20085, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KwKATGfft9CLGcyYL34ZXW", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24420, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_019xyVWXHqJxDAzbLcV2W3fg", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt finished in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (and why it was promoted even though the RC was unhealthy in staging), and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback partway."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55020, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_019xyVWXHqJxDAzbLcV2W3fg", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55020, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019xyVWXHqJxDAzbLcV2W3fg", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57047, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016g4yj6ae7mp2uR9urAfWht", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57347, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016g4yj6ae7mp2uR9urAfWht", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57347, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016g4yj6ae7mp2uR9urAfWht", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63065, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001) describing what happened.\n\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1, the one deployed now, was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the system that runs rollouts. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished everywhere.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The service is healthy and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created. I didn't retry, so there's no duplicate and on-call wasn't paged twice. The incident lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed, and why it reached production when its release candidate was unhealthy in staging.\n  - Look into the error that stopped the first rollback partway.\n\nNo approval was needed, because the policy only covers deploying versions that have never been healthy in production, and v2.3.0 has been.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NVh8GynMMahTvqDVn9nMLU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JqGjD3V3JR8NQS1DmNSt8D", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011X8USADUsBaWi2DrniGhhU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KzyZBKpAaVtDbQP4ezymfb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback failed partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll try the same rollback once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WXpdc8mNpfMXgZfHvwJnNX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KwKATGfft9CLGcyYL34ZXW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019xyVWXHqJxDAzbLcV2W3fg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt finished in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (and why it was promoted even though the RC was unhealthy in staging), and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback partway."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request to create the incident timed out. I'll check whether it was created anyway so I don't page twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016g4yj6ae7mp2uR9urAfWht", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001) describing what happened.\n\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1, the one deployed now, was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the system that runs rollouts. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished everywhere.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The service is healthy and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created. I didn't retry, so there's no duplicate and on-call wasn't paged twice. The incident lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed, and why it reached production when its release candidate was unhealthy in staging.\n  - Look into the error that stopped the first rollback partway.\n\nNo approval was needed, because the policy only covers deploying versions that have never been healthy in production, and v2.3.0 has been.", "type": "text"}]}]}